          "date": "2026-11-23 01:59:31.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20687 libcfs: report a bad pointer in container_of_safe()",
        "message": "LU-20687 libcfs: report a bad pointer in container_of_safe()\n\ncontainer_of_safe() returns an ERR_PTR() or NULL pointer unchanged.\nNo caller should ever pass one, but today this is silent and the bad\npointer is only noticed later, far from the cause.\n\nPrint an error and call dump_stack() when the pointer is bad.\nAlways use the libcfs macro instead of the one that some kernels\nprovide, so the check is present on every kernel.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2\nChange-Id: I3f1a60d601b6526246b54950fb9cc3ff6a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
